https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=megY_67DHCo  (Capo 0)

TIP:  If transposing, play the root chord of the transposed (Gadd) adding the 5th note as necessary.

TIP:  The intro are the chords from the chorus and the bridge is the "penny whistle" part.  It's kind of a you know it or you don't kind of proposition.  The notes at the end of the bridge are the first 7 notes to the "Old Spice" commercial.

TIP:  In the last verse the line that goes:  "Come next April I'm sixty-three", this line is sung on the up-inflection from start to finish so start "come" and finish "three" both on "high d".

TIP:  The chorus that has two "wily"s you'll see a bracketed |D| meaning strum once at that point.

TIP:  For the end notes on the outro (which may or may not transpose) you'll end on an (G) and that covered 1st string (g).  So keep the bottom finger on that covered (g) and just slide down one fret to the (f#) and back up to the (g) and the next note, (d) is right above it on the 2nd string/3rd fret and pick the (c) etc, finishing with a single strum of |G|. 
  
   
